// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO21/35/36/39-41 - dedicated onboard TFT
// display + shared SPI bus. Confirmed via vendor pins_arduino.h
// (TFT_BACKLIGHT=21,MOSI=35,SCK=36,TFT_DC=39,TFT_CS=40,TFT_RESET=41):
// https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/blob/master/variants/adafruit_funhouse_esp32s2/pins_arduino.h
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0/3/4/5 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard buttons
// (PIN_BUTTON4/BOOT0=0, PIN_BUTTON1/BUTTON_DOWN=3, PIN_BUTTON2/
// BUTTON_SELECT=4, PIN_BUTTON3/BUTTON_UP=5, per vendor pins_arduino.h and
// https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-funhouse/pinouts ).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO37 tagged "led_high" - CORRECTED. Previously lumped
// into the "35-37 dedicated TFT SPI bus" exclusion, but vendor
// pins_arduino.h shows GPIO37 is LED_BUILTIN (the SPI MISO line is
// unused by this write-only ST7789 display, so Adafruit reused it as the
// onboard red LED). Confirmed onboard/user-controllable and active-high
// via https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-funhouse/pinouts ("a red LED
// ... This LED is attached to LED or GPIO37") and
// https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-funhouse/arduino-basics
// (digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, HIGH) turns it on).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO14/15 excluded - CORRECTED. Previously left as plain
// GPIO, but vendor pins_arduino.h defines PIN_DOTSTAR_DATA=14 and
// PIN_DOTSTAR_CLOCK=15, and https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-funhouse/pinouts
// confirms "There are 4 DotStar LEDs on pin IO #14 and #15" - dedicated
// onboard addressable-LED driver pins, not general purpose (same
// treatment as this repo's adafruit_sparklemotionstick_esp32 DotStar
// exclusion precedent).
